# Build output
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
artifacts/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local databases.
#
# Never committed. These hold real-shaped birth records, registrar PIN
# hashes and audit rows; a civil registry's data does not belong in version
# control even when it is test data, because test data in a registry is
# indistinguishable in shape from the real thing.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Certificate signing material.
#
# The private key that signs birth certificates must never be generated into
# the repository or committed (see CLAUDE.md). A key in git history is a key
# that has to be treated as compromised, and every certificate it ever signed
# with it.
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
!**/testdata/*.pem

# Secrets
appsettings.*.local.json
*.env
.env
.env.*
secrets.json

# ...but the template must be committed, or a fresh clone cannot start the
# stack at all: compose refuses to run without the variables it names.
!.env.example

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Backups and dumps produced by the recovery drill (WS-A6)
*.dump
*.bak
backup/

# Front end (web/)
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Generated API client — regenerated from OpenAPI in CI.
# Not ignored: it is checked in deliberately, so a contract change shows up
# as a reviewable diff rather than as a silent difference between two
# machines. Delete this note, not the rule, if that decision is revisited.
